---
import ArchitectureFigure from "../../components/ArchitectureFigure.astro";
import DocsLayout from "../../components/DocsLayout.astro";

const lifecycle = [
    { title: "Sign in + open Setup", body: "You authenticate with Google, and the sandbox is created for you. The platform reserves a private tunnel and hands you a connect one-liner." },
    { title: "Connect", body: "You run the one-liner on your machine. It starts the sandbox, which dials out to make itself reachable and announces its URL to the platform on boot." },
    { title: "Bind on first use", body: "Your browser drives the daemon directly with your Google ID token. The daemon verifies it and binds you as owner on the first authenticated request." },
    { title: "Chat + plan", body: "You work over the tunnel: chat, files, editor, terminals. The agent runs in plan mode, proposing changes while you watch and steer." },
    { title: "Review + approve", body: "Every change comes back as a diff you commit or discard, and the agent can operate any connected system or tool from chat. You supervise; it does the work." },
];
---

<DocsLayout
    pageId="architecture"
    heading="Architecture"
    lead="intentic is two tiers: a thin platform for identity, and a per-agent sandbox on your hardware. Only the sandbox ever holds your code. It's where the agent, your workspace, and everything it can do actually live."
>
    <h2>The two tiers</h2>
    {/* The same figure the overview opens with, deliberately: a reader who followed the link from there should
        recognise the picture they arrived on, and the two pages describing one architecture with two different
        drawings of it was the reason to draw it properly once. */}
    <div class="docs-embed my-8">
        <ArchitectureFigure />
    </div>

    <h3>The platform</h3>
    <p>
        A thin hub: a Vue SPA and a small API. It persists your account, your subscription, and your sandbox's public URL, which the{" "}
        <a href="/docs/glossary/">daemon</a> announces on boot. It never probes the sandbox, owns no infrastructure, and sits <strong>off the command path</strong>: a platform
        breach can read a URL and reaches nothing else.
    </p>

    <h3>The sandbox</h3>
    <p>
        One container per agent, on your PC or your server, run <strong>unprivileged by default</strong>. It runs the coding agent, holds your repos and credentials, and exposes its daemon over its own tunnel. That is the whole product surface: chat, terminals, files, panels, capabilities and automations all come from here, and your keys never reach the platform. Inside it the agent runs whatever a job needs (a database client, a headless browser, a deployment engine), but those are tools it invokes, not tiers of the product.
    </p>

    <h2>Ownership &amp; trust</h2>
    <p>
        The trust root is your browser's Google sign-in. Your browser drives the daemon directly with a Google ID token; the daemon verifies
        it against Google's keys and binds you as owner on first use. <strong>The platform never holds that token</strong>, so it cannot drive your sandbox even if breached. Repos, credentials and history live where the sandbox runs, and capability secrets echo back to the UI only as "set" or "not set", never as values.
    </p>

    <h2>Reachability</h2>
    <p>
        Every connection is <strong>outbound-only</strong>. A small tunnel agent inside the sandbox dials out from your machine, so the sandbox is reachable from any browser with no inbound ports and no firewall changes. Its address comes from intentic's own tunnel hub — a per-sandbox grant the box enables with itself, which the platform can revoke but never use to serve anything in your name. Already publishing a sandbox under your own domain? Attach it by address instead, and nothing is provisioned at all.
    </p>

    <h2>The lifecycle</h2>
    <ol class="docs-embed my-6 list-none space-y-4 p-0">
        {
            lifecycle.map((step, i) => (
                <li class="flex gap-4">
                    <span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-primary-500/40 text-sm font-semibold text-link">
                        {i + 1}
                    </span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="text-sm font-medium text-content">{step.title}</div>
                        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{step.body}</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            ))
        }
    </ol>
</DocsLayout>
